<servcat id="01">
<name>Engine</name>
<section id="10024_S000T" variety="S000T">
<name>Starting</name>
<ttl id="10024_S000T_744HN_T007Z" variety="T007Z">
<name>Smart Entry &amp; Start System (Start System)</name>
<para id="X39400000IA00RC" category="C" type-id="304MY" name-id="161XA-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>B2275</dtccode>
<dtcname>Starter Circuit Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="X39400000IA00RC_10" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000049P00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>This DTC is output when a malfunction such as an open or short in the engine start request output circuit inside the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) is detected.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When using the TaSCAN with the IG OFF, repeatedly turn any door courtesy light switch ON and OFF (at intervals of 1.5 seconds or less) until communication between the TaSCAN and the vehicle starts.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The Smart Entry &amp; Start System (start system) has functions that use multiplex communication. First, follow "How to Proceed with Troubleshooting" and confirm that there is no malfunction in the communication system before proceeding with troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>When the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) is replaced with a new ECU and the battery negative terminal is connected, it enters the IG ON state. Also, when the battery is removed and reinstalled, the power source returns to the state it was in when the battery was removed.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1" pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="01" colname="C01" colwidth="1.01in"/>
<colspec colnum="02" colname="C02" colwidth="2.17in"/>
<colspec colnum="03" colname="C03" colwidth="3.90in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B2275</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="left">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Malfunction in the engine start request output circuit inside the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU), or external circuit malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry colname="C03" valign="middle" align="left">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Instrument Panel J/B Assembly (Main Body ECU)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>EFI System</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wire Harness or Connector</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000IA00RC_11" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000049Q00000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A161587J01" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000IA00RC_12" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000IA00RC_14" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="X39400000IA00RC_14_0013" proc-id="RM0550J___000049R00000">
<testtitle>Check DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Clear the DTCs.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the IG ON, depress the brake pedal, check the DTCs again after 15 seconds or more have elapsed, and check that no DTC is output.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.30in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.83in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC is output again</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>No DTC is output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000IA00RC_14_0015" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="X39400000IA00RC_14_0018" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000IA00RC_14_0015" proc-id="RM0550J___000049T00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness (Instrument Panel J/B Assembly (Main Body ECU) - Engine Control Computer (Engine ECU))</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Resistance Inspection</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A161588J01" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>Disconnect instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) connector T and engine control computer (engine ECU) connector B.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), inspect the resistance between the terminals of the vehicle side wire harness connector.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" rowsep="1" align="center">
<colspec colnum="1" colname="C01" colwidth="2.69in"/>
<colspec colnum="2" colname="COLSPEC0" colwidth="0.70in"/>
<colspec colnum="3" colname="C02" colwidth="0.74in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle">
<ptxt>Terminal No.</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Main Body ECU - Engine ECU)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle">
<ptxt>T4(STSW) - B14(STSW)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), inspect the resistance between each terminal of the vehicle side wire harness connector and body ground.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<tgroup cols="3" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="1" colname="C01" colwidth="2.68in"/>
<colspec colnum="2" colname="COLSPEC1" colwidth="0.71in"/>
<colspec colnum="3" colname="C02" colwidth="0.74in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Terminal No.</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Main Body ECU or Engine ECU - Body Ground)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>T4 (STSW) or B14 (STSW) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>10k Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000IA00RC_14_0014" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="X39400000IA00RC_14_0019" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000IA00RC_14_0014" proc-id="RM0550J___000049S00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Instrument Panel J/B Assembly (Main Body ECU)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Voltage Inspection</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A161589J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>Connect the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) connector.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage between the terminal and body ground from the back side of the instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU) connector.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The STSW output voltage is output for 300ms at the moment the engine starts.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</test2>
</test1>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.48in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.59in"/>
<colspec colname="COL4" colwidth="1.06in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Terminal No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>T4 (STSW) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Brake pedal depressed, engine switch held pushed</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>{ (AM1 or AM2) - 2V} or more</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000IA00RC_14_0017" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="X39400000IA00RC_14_0020" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000IA00RC_14_0017">
<testtitle>Go to EFI System<xref label="Seep01" href="X39400000QQ017D"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000IA00RC_14_0018">
<testtitle>Perform Simulation Method<xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000IA00RC_14_0019">
<testtitle>Repair or Replace Wire Harness or Connector</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000IA00RC_14_0020">
<testtitle>Replace instrument panel J/B assembly (main body ECU)</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
